# TimeTracker — Project Rules & Memory

## What this app is
A native macOS menu bar time tracker. No Dock icon. No screenshots. No activity monitoring.
Just a timer with start/stop, manual time entry, and daily/weekly/monthly statistics.

## Stack
- Swift + SwiftUI, minimum macOS 13
- Swift Package Manager (no Xcode project)
- Run with: `swift run` | Build: `swift build -c release`

## Architecture

### Entry point
`main.swift` — creates `NSApplication`, sets `.accessory` activation policy (hides Dock icon), attaches `AppDelegate`, calls `app.run()`.
Do NOT use `@main` App struct — it conflicts with `main.swift`.

### AppDelegate
Owns the `NSStatusItem` and the `NSPanel` popup.
- Status bar button image is a custom-drawn `NSImage` (non-template) with pill border, colored icon and time text.
- Popup is an `NSPanel` (`.borderless` + `.nonactivatingPanel`) with `NSVisualEffectView` (`.popover` material, corner radius 12) as content background.
- Panel is positioned flush below the menu bar button using `button.window?.convertToScreen(...)` + `setFrameTopLeftPoint`.
- Panel dismissal: global `NSEvent` monitor (clicks outside) + `NSApplication.didResignActiveNotification` (Cmd+Tab / app switch). Both are removed in `closePanel()`.

### TimerManager (singleton)
`TimerManager.shared` — `ObservableObject`.
- `start()` / `stop()` / `reset()` / `addTime(hours:minutes:)`.
- On `stop()`: records the delta since last save as a `TimeSession` in `SessionStore`.
- On `addTime()`: records a manual `TimeSession` immediately.
- `loadTodayTime()` — called once at launch to seed `elapsedSeconds` with today's already-tracked total.

### SessionStore (singleton)
`SessionStore.shared` — `ObservableObject`.
- Persists to `~/Library/Application Support/TimeTracker/sessions.json` (ISO-8601 dates).
- Key queries: `sessions(on:)`, `sessions(weekOffset:)`, `sessions(monthOffset:)`, `totalSeconds(in:)`.

### Menu bar icon colors
- **Idle** (no time): `labelColor` (adapts to light/dark)
- **Running**: `systemGreen`
- **Paused with time**: `systemOrange`
Icon is drawn with `NSImage.SymbolConfiguration(paletteColors:)` to bake color in.
Text is drawn via `NSAttributedString` with explicit `.foregroundColor`.
Everything (icon + time) is inside a pill drawn with `NSBezierPath(roundedRect:)`.

### ContentView tabs
Timer tab | Stats tab — `Picker` with `.segmented` style.

### StatsView
- Always shows "Today" total at top.
- `Picker` for Week / Month.
- `‹ label ⌄ ›` navigation row: arrows step ±1, label is a `Menu` dropdown listing all periods with data.
- Week/month offsets are independent state (switching tabs preserves position).
- Future navigation disabled (`offset >= 0`).

## Key patterns
- SF Symbol coloring in off-screen `NSImage`: use `NSImage.SymbolConfiguration(paletteColors:)` — NOT `contentTintColor`, NOT `attributedTitle`, NOT `destinationIn` compositing.
- `MenuBarExtra` label colors are stripped by macOS — always use `NSStatusItem` with custom-drawn `NSImage` for colored menu bar items.
- `onChange(of:)` — use single-arg form `{ newValue in }` for macOS 13 compatibility. Two-arg form `{ _, new in }` requires macOS 14+.

## Git workflow
- Every new feature or bug fix MUST be developed on a dedicated branch created from `main`.
- Branch naming: `feature/<short-description>` or `fix/<short-description>`.
- Once work is complete, push the branch and open a pull/merge request against `main`.
- Direct commits to `main` are not allowed.
